{t: Cissy Strut}
{st: The Meters}
{key: C}
{tempo: 88}

{sot: Head}
| C7          | C7          | C7          | C7          |
| C7          | C7          | C7          | C7          |
{eot}

{sot: Bridge}
| Ab7   G7    | C7          | Ab7   G7    | C7          |
{eot}

{sot: Solo}
| C7          | C7          | C7          | C7          |
{eot}

{sov: Notes}
New Orleans Funk: Built on Leo Nocentelli's classic syncopated guitar riff and
Zigaboo Modeliste's iconic second-line drum groove in C Dorian / C Mixolydian.

Head Riff: The main theme relies on single-note guitar and organ unisons rather
than heavy strumming. Keep the right-hand feel tight and heavily syncopated.

Bridge Stabs: The bridge section features sharp chromatic dominant stabs on Ab7
and G7 that resolve cleanly back into the main C7 groove.

Rhythm Pocket: Use muted 16th-note scratch fill-ins between line phrases and
favor top-string shell voicings for any rhythm chord stabs.
{eov}